     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This dose is double the IR maximum. It would raise the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**: for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**: a more typical regimen.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and whether it should be IR or ER. I'll enter it once you do. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and give a rationale for the order note. I'd still recommend a pharmacist review first."
      }
     ],
